# Explicit trusted registry. Without this, install falls back to whatever
# registry.npmjs.org (or an environment-injected NPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY /
# alternate .npmrc higher up the filesystem) happens to resolve to - pinning
# it removes that ambiguity rather than relying on an implicit default.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/

# NOTE: engine-strict=true was tried and reverted here - it fails locally
# because a transitive dependency (jsdom@30) requires Node ^22.22.2 and this
# machine has 22.22.0, one patch version short. The project's own
# engines.node (>=22) is satisfied; the stricter transitive requirement is
# pnpm's normal (non-fatal) warning today. Enabling engine-strict would turn
# that warning into a hard install failure on this machine, which is a
# regression, not a hardening - left off until the Node version is bumped.
